{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The maximum magnitude outcome for both Lottery A and Lottery B is the highest positive payout, since both have 0 as the lowest outcome. For Lottery A, the maximum magnitude outcome is 2400 Euros with a probability of 34%. For Lottery B, it is 2500 Euros with a probability of 33%. The reason evaluates which lottery has the more favorable (i.e., higher) maximum magnitude outcome weighted by its probability. The weighted values are: Lottery A: 2400 × 0.34 = 816; Lottery B: 2500 × 0.33 = 825. Since 825 > 816, the decision reason would prefer Lottery B.",
