{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. Both lotteries involve only gains (no losses), so the maximum magnitude outcome for each is simply the highest possible gain. For Lottery A, this is 3000 Euros with a probability of 25%. For Lottery B, it is 4000 Euros with a probability of 20%. The reason evaluates which lottery has the more favorable (i.e., higher expected value of) maximum magnitude outcome, which here would be the product of the highest outcome and its probability: 3000 × 0.25 = 750 for A, and 4000 × 0.20 = 800 for B. Since 800 > 750, the reason would prefer Lottery B.",
